kernelsu-dkms for Debian
========================

This package ships the KernelSU kernel module as a DKMS source tree in
/usr/src/kernelsu-<version>. DKMS rebuilds the module whenever a new kernel
or new kernel headers are installed.

Getting the module built
------------------------
The postinst builds the module for every installed kernel that has matching
headers under /lib/modules/<kver>/build, not just the running kernel. A
kernel without headers is skipped; to cover it, install its headers and run:

    sudo apt install linux-headers-<kver>
    sudo dkms autoinstall

dkms.conf sets AUTOINSTALL="yes", so DKMS also builds the module
automatically when new kernel headers are installed later. Check the result
with:

    dkms status -m kernelsu
    sudo modprobe ksu

GXDE 6.6 kernels backport anon_inode_create_getfile (mainline 6.8) and the
four-argument change_pid (mainline 6.15). The DKMS sources installed by this
package have the matching version gates lowered so those kernels build
correctly. On a stock mainline kernel without these backports the build can
still fail; the postinst reports such kernels without aborting installation.

Installed files
---------------
  /usr/src/kernelsu-<version>/         DKMS module sources and dkms.conf
  /usr/bin/kernelsu-loader             ksuinit userspace helper
  /usr/bin/load-kernelsu               loads the module through modloader
  /etc/modprobe.d/00-kernelsu.conf     makes "ksu" an alias of "kernelsu"

load-kernelsu needs the optional "modloader" utility and root privileges.
Use "load-kernelsu --unload-first" to reload an already loaded module.
